   "value": "catdS10",
   "variant_id": "h33-h33-2-b2-CONCENTRATIONcatdS10-20261024-6b87f2d7",
   "hypothesis": "Mirror image of catd10, built because the previous session's IRREGULARITIES entry requires both directions before a CONCENTRATION result can be read as a sign. It moves the same 10% of dots between the same 1 km blocks in the opposite direction, so a monotone (catd10 > R0 > catdS10) or inverted (catdS10 > R0 > catd10) response identifies the sign of the catalogue-density prior; a flat response on both sides says the metric is insensitive to km-scale reallocation at this count.",
   "mechanism": "Same fixed-S bookkeeping as catd10 with donor and receiver block sets swapped. If the known-structure-density prior is informative, this variant must LOSE: it takes the most truth-dense dots away and re-places them where known structure is absent. Its predicted loss is therefore as informative as catd10's predicted gain.",
